Parts of alrust derived from Alerta, changed for Rust and PostgreSQL:
- the alert lifecycle state machine (crates/alrust-engine), ported from
  alerta/models/alarms/alerta.py;
- the reference PostgreSQL schema embedded in
  crates/alrust-store-pg/migrations/0002_reference_layout.sql and
  crates/alrust-store-pg/reference-catalog.json, from
  alerta/database/backends/postgres/schema.sql;
- the API behaviour, query handling and webhook mappings specified in spec/
  and implemented in crates/, from the Alerta server sources.

The Alerta sources are kept unchanged, for reference only, under
reference/alerta and reference/alerta-webui (both Apache-2.0).

Third-party Rust crates keep their own licences; their texts and notices are
under third_party/rust.
